{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "verifiedThrough": "2026-09-16",
  "note": "Expected-engagement factor per normal tower, transcribed from the developer-linked Element TD 2 DPS/Gold workbook. factor = (chosen row's DPS) ÷ (base row's SDPS). The workbook's DPS column already averages single-target and area damage (SDPS × (1 + AoE Mult) / 2) and, on an '(Average)' row, the tower's duty cycle (Golem's average row carries a third of its active damage). The base row is the plain row when present, else the variant whose SDPS is closest to the catalog's damage × attack speed (Golem's '(Active)', Laser's '(Max)'), so the ratio is measured against the stat line the catalog actually carries. Taking the ratio inside the workbook keeps data/towers.v2.json as the authority for current damage and attack speed (the workbook's absolute damage predates 1.9.4 for some towers). Row policy: '(Average)' when present, else the plain row, else the variant with the LOWEST ratio (conservative — Laser is credited at its non-isolated '(Min)' damage; isolation providers are not credited yet). This is the same convention data/earlyTowerCombat.v1.json already carries for single-element towers. All rows are listed for audit. isolatedEngagementFactor (Laser, Incantation only): the workbook row for the isolated case — Laser '(Max)', Incantation '(With Full Amp)' — over the same base SDPS; the survival model uses it only while a verified target-isolation provider (Rage) is fielded within reach of the tower.",
  "sources": [
    "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1GdfCqVeudiNHhxHF1XYSUMqkyNRRkCx-loXJiNQqv4s/edit?usp=sharing"
  ],
  "convention": "averageDps = damage × attacksPerSecond × engagementFactor",
